  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through Monday)\nIssued at 1130 PM CDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nThings clear out through the middle part of the week as generally\nzonal flow aloft develops over much of the southern CONUS. A\ntightening pressure gradient on Wednesday will provide an uptick\nin wind speeds, which along with the dry conditions and warm\ntemperatures in the 80s will raise fire weather concerns Wednesday\nafternoon. Conditions will remain well below critical levels\nhowever.\n\nWarm and dry conditions continue into Thursday, before a more\nunsettled weather pattern develops by late week into the weekend.\nThere continues to be noticeable uncertainty in the guidance as \nto the evolution of the impactful systems during this time frame. \nIn general though, we can expect a break down of the upper level \nridge with stronger western troughing and southwest flow aloft \ndeveloping over the Southern Plains. Various shortwaves look to \nmove through the flow through the weekend into early next week, \nwhich along with increasing lower level moisture will bring better\nrain chances along with some thunderstorm potential. The first \nsystem is on track for late Friday into Saturday at the present \ntime with a possible stronger wave and frontal boundary pushing \nthrough Sunday night into Monday. A robust upper low could linger \nin the area through the first part of next week bringing lingering\nrain chances along with at least a modest airmass change back to \nnear normal conditions.\n\nBowlan",
